    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0214" n="106" xml:id="pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/8625: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-08T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1927—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 8—6:25
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>388. My No. 359, April 6, 10 a.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Foreign commandants at conference, Tientsin, April 6, unanimously
                        expressed the opinion that the more troops on the spot the less likely the
                        necessity will be to take military action and they submitted that to this
                        end an increase of the garrisons in North China to 25,000 men forthwith
                        would be the best solution. They agreed to transmit this opinion to their
                        respective Ministers.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I concur.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
